<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Torarica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Torarica was the capital of the English colony of Willoughbyland on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname-river">Suriname River</a>, a small town of planters founded in the 1650s. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> conquest of 1667 the seat of government moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paramaribo">Paramaribo</a>, nearer the coast, and Torarica declined. It was later abandoned, and little trace of it remains.</p></div>
